  "prefLabel": "Plc 1406.14 Professional Presentations",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1406.14 Professional Presentations.\n\n(a) A licensee may claim credit towards the continuing competence requirement for a professional presentation at a professional symposium, conference, or workshop, provided that:\n\n(1) The licensee is the primary presenter; and\n\n(2) The content of the presentation relates directly to one or more of the NCTRC knowledge domains.\n\n(b) The licensee may claim one hour for each clock hour of the presentation to a maximum of 10 hours per renewal cycle.\n\n(c) The licensee shall not claim credit for multiple or repeat presentations of the same material, provided that the licensee may claim credit for a presentation of the same topic in a subsequent renewal cycle if the licensee has substantially revised the presentation materials.\n\n(d) Documentation of a licensee’s professional presentation at a professional symposium, conference, or workshop shall be:\n\n(1) The printed program of the symposium, conference, or workshop showing:\n\na. A description of the subject(s) of the presentation;\n\nb. The date of the presentation;\n\nc. The number of hours of the presentation; and\n\nd. If the licensee previously claimed credit for a presentation on the same topic, a written explanation of the revisions made by the licensee to the materials presented; and\n\n(2) A copy of:\n\na. An evaluation of the presentation;\n\nb. A summary of the evaluations of the presentation;\n\nc. A letter of thanks specifically identifying the presentation and addressed to the licensee; or\n\nd. Any other document confirming that the presentation was completed.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Plc 1400) #13705, eff 8-1-23; ss by #14442, eff 1-26-26, EXPIRES 1-26-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1400.html"
}
